 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-specialtydirectory-001"></a>
+
+<!-- Requested by the product owner on 2026-08-15, not derived from observed behavior. -->
+
+Staff also ask the veterinarian directory's question in reverse: which veterinarians hold a given specialty. A second page answers it. That page lists every specialty the clinic knows, each under its stored name, together with the veterinarians holding it. Each of those veterinarians is named in full, first name then last name. Every specialty is shown on the one page, with no paging. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on the page, because the page lists specialties rather than the whole roster. The page is reached by its own address, and nothing links to it `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]`.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every one is listed under its stored name on a single page.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a specialty that veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened, then each holder is named by first name followed by last name.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is not shown anywhere on it.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the directory's own address, when it is requested directly, then the page is shown, while no other page and no navigation offers a way to it.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty that no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian shown against it.
+2. Specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+3. When the clinic knows no specialty at all, the page is shown as an empty directory rather than failing.
+4. The page's own wording is subject to `REQ-LANG-002`; the stored specialty names and veterinarian names are data and are shown as held.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
